---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
---
<Base title="About" description="Who runs EarlySpawn, how codes and guides are sourced, and what our Tested and Not tested labels mean.">
  <div class="wrap prose page">
    <h1>About {site.name}</h1>
    <p>{site.name} covers Roblox games that are gaining players, with codes, beginner guides, and game info in one place.</p>

    <h2>Who runs this</h2>
    <p>{site.name} is run by one person. AI tools help draft and maintain pages, and that isn't hidden. A person decides what gets published, and fixes anything reported as wrong. We'd rather say "we don't know yet" than guess.</p>

    <h2>How codes are sourced</h2>
    <p>Codes come from a game's in-game code list, its Roblox page, the developer's announcements, or a community wiki. Every code shows where it came from and one of two labels:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Tested</strong>, with a date: we redeemed that code in Roblox ourselves on that day.</li>
      <li><strong>Not tested</strong>: the source lists it as active, but we haven't redeemed it yet.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The "Code list reviewed" date at the top of a codes page is the last time a person went through that list. It doesn't mean every code was redeemed that day. Codes that stop working move to the expired list instead of quietly disappearing, and when a game has no working codes we say so.</p>

    <h2>How guides are sourced</h2>
    <p>Each guide says at the top whether we tested it ourselves or put it together from other players' guides and videos, and names the sources where we can. Anything no one has confirmed is marked unconfirmed.</p>

    <h2>Suggestions and corrections</h2>
    <p>Want a game covered, a guide written, or spotted something wrong? Send it through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>

    <h2>Business enquiries</h2>
    <p>For sponsorships, partnerships, press, or anything from a game developer, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. That address is for business only.</p>

    <p>{site.name} is a fan site. It isn't affiliated with or endorsed by Roblox Corporation or any game developer.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
<style>.page { padding-top: 36px; } .page h1 { margin-bottom: 18px; }</style>
